# CS-14 (audit S1-002): the malware incident rewrote commits with CRLF line
# endings, which hid the real change inside whole-file diffs. Store text as LF
# so a line-ending flip can no longer mask a payload in review.
#
# This file only sets the policy. Existing files are NOT renormalised here
# (that would be a huge, unreviewable diff); files already committed with CRLF
# keep it until they are next edited. A one-off `git add --renormalize .` can
# be done later as its own reviewed commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary: never convert or diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.mov binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.wasm binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.exe binary
